                <note rend="inline" type="source">655.116 Auto/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-21T14:00:00-05:00">November 21, 1935—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. Your 92, November 20, 6 p.m. Culbertson, now in Paris, has been directed to
                    proceed at once to Brussels to consult with you and appropriate Belgian
                    officials concerning the proposed tire quota. Since he was a negotiator of the
                    Belgian trade agreement, the Department would like to have his recommendations
                    before deciding upon its course of action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
